
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cp-g5-disposicoes-finais`

-- Independent tests, ta-g5, Disposições Finais (arts. 360 and 361): cases
-- IT-g5-228 to IT-g5-232 of ~/.claude/br-penal-oracle/cases/ta-g5.json
-- (sha256 fd67bfdc…, frozen 2026-09-29 before the encoding was read).
--
-- The encoding carries both articles as the Code's words only (two STRING
-- constants, `cp-g5-disposicoes-finais.l4`): the brief classes a revocation
-- clause and a vigência clause as inert. None of the five cases asks for the
-- words; each asks a question the words answer, and no rule computes it. So
-- all five are NOT-EXPRESSIBLE, and this module has no directive.

§ `Testes independentes de ta-g5 — Disposições Finais`

-- IT-g5-228: NOT-EXPRESSIBLE — O art. 360 revogou a legislação especial sobre crimes
-- militares? Art. 360 is a STRING; no rule says what it revokes or saves.

-- IT-g5-229: NOT-EXPRESSIBLE — O art. 360 revogou a legislação especial sobre os crimes
-- de falência? Same reason.

-- IT-g5-230: NOT-EXPRESSIBLE — Essa disposição foi revogada pelo art. 360? Same reason.

-- IT-g5-231: NOT-EXPRESSIBLE — Em que data o Código Penal entrou em vigor? Art. 361 is a
-- STRING; the encoding has no DATE for 1.1.1942 (grep of every module: "1942" occurs
-- only in that string and its test).

-- IT-g5-232: NOT-EXPRESSIBLE — O Código Penal de 1940 estava em vigor na data do fato
-- (15.12.1941)? No gate reads art. 361, by design (the module's header: "no fact before
-- 1942 is asked about, so a gate on this date would decide nothing").
